    "# 3. Data\n",
    "Data section (Salwa Majeed)\n",
    "\n",
    "Source: Chicago Data Portal, Traffic Crashes, Crashes dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "What we did: We downloaded 1,108,694 crash records. We removed duplicates and rows with no injury information, leaving 1,106,297. We kept crashes from 2018 onward because earlier years (2013 to 2017) have far fewer records, which suggests incomplete reporting. That left 968,596 crashes from 2018 through October 2026 (2026 is a partial year).\n",
    "\n",
    "Cleaning: We turned UNKNOWN values into blanks, set impossible coordinates (0) to blank, and set speed limits outside 5 to 70 mph to blank. After cleaning, about 5.2 percent of rows are missing lighting, 6.5 percent are missing weather, 0.5 percent are missing speed limit, and about 0.8 percent are missing coordinates.\n",
    "\n",
    "New columns: severe (1 if the crash had a fatal or incapacitating injury, 0 otherwise), any_injury, hit_and_run, and crash_year. About 1.79 percent of crashes are severe.\n",
    "\n",
    "Limits: The data has no traffic volume, so we compare severity rates and not crash counts. Freeway crashes are largely missing, and only reported crashes are included. The newest crashes may be missing later fatality updates.\n",
    "\n",
    "Cleaning code: see notebooks/salwa_data_and_stats.ipynb in the repository.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Other data we added (name the owner):**"
   ]
