   "source": [
    "EDA note (Salwa): Crashes follow a clear daily pattern. They are lowest in the early morning, at about 11,000 crashes at 4 am, then jump at 7 and 8 am with the morning commute. They dip slightly around 9 and 10 am, then climb through the day and peak in the mid to late afternoon, at about 75,000 crashes at 3 pm and almost as many at 4 and 5 pm. After 6 pm they fall steadily into the night. The busiest hour has roughly six to seven times as many crashes as the quietest one. This matters for our analysis for two reasons. First, because far fewer crashes happen at night, a rate (the share of crashes that are severe or hit and run) is a fairer comparison than a raw count. Second, our later results about nighttime, such as the higher hit and run share after dark, describe a larger share of a much smaller number of crashes."
   ]
